## Other queries

```graphql
query {
  tesla {
  session(id: "SESSION_ID") {
      id displayName mapName createdAt lastActionAt
      gameState { playerPos { x y } battery score victory gameOver }
      gameMap { name gridSize maxBattery startingBattery }
    }
  }
}
```

```graphql
query {
  tesla {
  sessions(sort: ACTION, order: DESC, limit: 20) {
      count total sort order
      sessions { id displayName mapName lastActionAt gameState { victory gameOver score battery } }
    }
  }
}
```

`sort`: `ACTION` (last move, default) or `CREATED`. `order`: `ASC` or `DESC`.

```graphql
query {
  tesla {
  unifiedSessions(mapName: "easy") {
      mapName count
      sessions {
        sessionId createdAt lastActionAt
        gameState { playerPos { x y } battery score victory gameOver }
        gameMap { name gridSize maxBattery }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

```graphql
query {
  tesla {
  history(sessionID: "SESSION_ID", page: 1, limit: 20, order: DESC) {
      totalMoves totalPages hasNext hasPrevious page pageSize
      moves { moveNumber action battery success timestamp fromPosition { x y } toPosition { x y } }
    }
  }
}
```

The `map(name: …)` query (full map config) and the MCP `get_map` tool are restricted to the web
UI and need a UI password. Agents should read the map through `gameState.grid` instead.

## Other mutations

```graphql
mutation {
  tesla {
  updateSession(id: "SESSION_ID", displayName: "Claude's first run") { id displayName }
  }
}
```

```graphql
mutation {
  tesla {
  deleteSession(id: "SESSION_ID") { message }
  }
}
```

```graphql
mutation {
  tesla {
  validateMap(map: {
      name: "Tiny"
      description: "Two parks"
      gridSize: 5
      maxBattery: 10
      startingBattery: 10
      layout: ["BBBBB", "BHRPB", "BRRRB", "BPRSB", "BBBBB"]
      legend: [
        { key: "R", value: "road" }, { key: "H", value: "home" }, { key: "P", value: "park" }
        { key: "S", value: "supercharger" }, { key: "B", value: "building" }, { key: "W", value: "water" }
      ]
    }) { valid winnable message error }
  }
}
```

`validateMap` needs no key and saves nothing. A map needs `gridSize` between 5 and 100, a square
layout of `gridSize` rows × `gridSize` characters, at least one H and one P, and a legend that
maps all six standard characters (R H P S B W) as shown. One-way cells are custom characters
declared in `cellConfigs`, e.g.
`cellConfigs: [{ key: ">", type: "road", allowedDirections: ["east"] }]`.

### Map administration

Map authoring needs a signed-in player (the global `account` sign-in); signed-out calls are
`UNAUTHENTICATED`.

| Mutation | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `createMap(name, map: GameMapInput)` | Creates a `DRAFT` owned by the caller. It never overwrites a shipped map. The response says `status: DRAFT`, `ownedByMe: true`, `builtin: false`. |
| `updateMap(name, patch: GameMapPatchInput)` | Owner-only. An edit puts the map back into `DRAFT`; patch fields are optional. |
| `publishMap(name)` | Owner-only; runs the full winnability gate (every park reachable) and moves the draft to `PUBLISHED`. |
| `deleteMap(name)` | Owner-only for the caller's own map. |
| `claimMap(name, editKey)` | One-time claim of a legacy ownerless map with the edit key it was created with. |
| `validateMap(map)` | Checks a map without saving it. |

Visibility follows the lifecycle: `maps` shows published maps plus your own drafts, and
`map(name)` returns `null` for another player's draft exactly like an unknown name. A `DRAFT`
cannot be played or published by anyone else.

Shipped maps are `builtin: true`, `PUBLISHED` and ownerless; changing or deleting one needs
`X-Admin-Key` equal to `TESLA_ADMIN_API_KEY`. A legacy ownerless custom map also needs the admin
key until `claimMap` attaches it to an account; after that its owner edits it without any key.

Custom maps live in PostgreSQL (`platform_maps`), capped by `TESLA_MAX_USER_MAPS` (default 200).
`TESLA_CUSTOM_MAPS_DIR` is not a runtime setting: existing custom maps are imported once with
`drbrain import-maps --game=tesla --dir=<legacy directory>`. Imported maps become `PUBLISHED`
and ownerless; use `claimMap` with the old edit key to attach them to an account. `pg_dump` is
the only backup for custom maps; builtin `maps/*.json` files stay release-managed.

